# =============================================================================
# PRIVON .gitignore
# Conservative: only ignore generated build/release output, local machine
# state, and local user data. Legitimate repository content (src/, tests/,
# docs/, tools/, server/) is never ignored here.
# =============================================================================

# --- .NET build output ------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# --- dotnet test results -----------------------------------------------------
TestResults/
*.trx

# --- Publish / release packaging output --------------------------------------
# tools/publish-release.ps1 stages and packages everything under release/.
# Nothing under here should ever be committed.
publish/
release/

# --- PRIVON diagnostic logs ---------------------------------------------------
# Metadata-only diagnostic log, opt-in via PRIVON_ENABLE_DIAGNOSTICS=1.
# Never contains raw PII, but is local machine/session state and must not be
# committed regardless.
privon-diagnostic-*.log

# --- PRIVON local user data ----------------------------------------------------
# Production storage lives under %LocalAppData%\PRIVON, not the repo. These
# patterns exist only as a safety net in case a local run/test ever writes
# encrypted local state into the working tree.
master.key
settings.bin
trusted-public-info.bin
exceptions.bin
user-exceptions.bin

# --- Editor / IDE local state --------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.suo
.obsidian/

# --- Claude Code local (machine-specific) settings ------------------------------
# .claude/settings.json (shared, if present) IS tracked; only the local
# per-machine override is ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- OS junk -------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- Internal engineering log (publication-scope decision, not a secret) -------
# CLAUDE.md is a large, highly granular internal development/workflow log. It has
# been privacy/secret-audited clean, but the product owner has decided it should
# not enter the public GitHub history -- public engineering documentation is
# instead represented by README.md/README.ko.md, docs/, CONTRIBUTING.md, and
# SECURITY.md. Root-only rule so other Markdown files (docs/, README variants,
# CONTRIBUTING.md, SECURITY.md) are never affected. The local file is kept for
# continued development use and is not deleted.
/CLAUDE.md
